vc.codex.hunter.become.1=Craft a §fSyringe§r (glass + iron) and combine it with §fGarlic§r to make a §eGarlic Syringe§r. Use it to take the oath.	#
vc.codex.hunter.become.2=Garlic grows on farmland and is found in village and dungeon chests.	#
vc.codex.hunter.become.title=Becoming a hunter	#
vc.codex.hunter.bow.1=Shoots fast blessed arrows (uses normal arrows). They burn supernatural creatures.	#
vc.codex.hunter.bow.2=Only hunters can use it. Tap and hold to shoot.	#
vc.codex.hunter.bow.title=Hunter's Bow	#
vc.codex.hunter.intro=§7Humans sworn to cleanse the world of darkness.	#
vc.codex.hunter.missions.1=Each rank requires a mission: hunt creatures or deliver relics. Hunting missions complete by themselves.	#
vc.codex.hunter.missions.2=Talk to the §eHunter Master§r or use the Insignia to deliver relics. Every mission gives rewards and 1 training point.	#
vc.codex.hunter.missions.title=Missions	#
vc.codex.hunter.skills.1=§fHunter's Sense§r (rank 2) reveals nearby supernaturals. §fDivine Protection§r (rank 5) creates a holy aura.	#
vc.codex.hunter.skills.2=§fHoly Burst§r (rank 8) burns everything supernatural around you.	#
vc.codex.hunter.skills.title=Skills	#
vc.codex.hunter.stats.1=§fVitality§r raises health, §fAgility§r speed and jump, and §fCombat§r damage against vampires and werewolves.	#
vc.codex.hunter.stats.2=Each attribute goes up to 8. Choose wisely: there are 10 missions in total.	#
vc.codex.hunter.stats.title=Training	#
vc.codex.intro=§7Everything you need to know about vampires, werewolves and hunters.	#
vc.codex.items.altar.1=Fills up with 10 full blood bottles or werewolf livers. When full, it accepts your race's offering.	#
vc.codex.items.altar.2=Each skill costs human hearts and vampire blood (dropped by hunters and vampires) and requires a minimum level.	#
vc.codex.items.altar.title=Blood Altar	#
vc.codex.items.armor.1=Made from Sunstone and Moonstone ingots, ores found underground.	#
vc.codex.items.armor.2=Set bonus (helmet + boots + chestplate and leggings of the same side): §6Solar§r — vampires become immune to the sun, others gain fire resistance. §9Lunar§r — night vision and strength at night; werewolves gain resistance.	#
vc.codex.items.armor.title=Eclipse Armor	#
vc.codex.items.coffin.1=Vampires and werewolves can use it as a bed: it sets your respawn point.	#
vc.codex.items.coffin.2=Used during the day, you sleep until night.	#
vc.codex.items.coffin.title=Coffin	#
vc.codex.items.cures.1=§dVampirism Cure§r and §dLycanthropy Cure§r restore your humanity (you lose levels and skills).	#
vc.codex.items.cures.2=At a crafting table: §bPhilosopher's Water§r = bottle + water bucket + Philosopher's Stone. Vampirism Cure = Philosopher's Water + Vampire Fang + Garlic. Lycanthropy Cure = Philosopher's Water + Werewolf Fang + Moonstone Ingot.	#
vc.codex.items.cures.title=Cures	#
vc.codex.items.grinder.1=4 identical raw meats + 1 glass bottle = 1 full blood bottle.	#
vc.codex.items.grinder.2=A peaceful way to feed without hunting.	#
vc.codex.items.grinder.title=Meat Grinder	#
vc.codex.items.intro=§7Tools, weapons and blocks.	#
vc.codex.items.recharge.1=The §dVampiric Sword§r and the §6Claws§r lose power with use (thirsty → drained).	#
vc.codex.items.recharge.2=Recharge at the §5Recharging Altar§r with 4 full bottles or 4 livers. Enchantments and names are kept.	#
vc.codex.items.recharge.title=Blood weapons	#
vc.codex.items.weapons.1=The §dVampiric Sword§r steals life with every hit (vampires also gain blood). The §6Werewolf Claws§r make targets bleed and hit harder in beast form.	#
vc.codex.items.weapons.2=Holding §fGarlic§r (either hand) weakens and slows vampires within 5 blocks. Vampires holding garlic get sick. Hunter's Bow: sticks + string + Sunstone Ingot.	#
vc.codex.items.weapons.title=Weapons and garlic	#
