vc.codex.title=§4Vampire Craft Codex	#
vc.codex.vampire.become.1=Use a §fVampire Fang§r (dropped by vampires) or get bitten by a vampire player.	#
vc.codex.vampire.become.2=The change takes 5 minutes and brings hunger and weakness. Drink §fmilk§r to cancel.	#
vc.codex.vampire.become.title=Becoming a vampire	#
vc.codex.vampire.bite.1=§fSneak and attack§r an animal, villager or human to bite it. A fangs icon appears on the HUD when a target is in range.	#
vc.codex.vampire.bite.2=Holding a §fglass bottle§r, bites fill bottles instead of drinking. Careful: hunters have garlic in their blood!	#
vc.codex.vampire.bite.title=Biting	#
vc.codex.vampire.blood.1=Vampires don't get hungry: they need §cblood§r (drops in the status bar). High blood regenerates you; low blood makes you slow and weak.	#
vc.codex.vampire.blood.2=With no blood you start dying. Drink §cBlood Bottles§r or bite creatures.	#
vc.codex.vampire.blood.title=Blood	#
vc.codex.vampire.intro=§7Immortal creatures of the night, driven by blood.	#
vc.codex.vampire.level.1=You earn experience by biting. There are 10 levels; each unlocks new powers at the altar and strengthens your body.	#
vc.codex.vampire.level.2=Level 3: speed. Level 4: strength at night. Level 5: more health. Level 8: strength II at night. Level 9: extra health. Level 10: the sun only sets you on fire, no extra damage.	#
vc.codex.vampire.level.title=Levels	#
vc.codex.vampire.skills.1=Awaken powers at the §4Blood Altar§r: fill it with 10 full bottles (or livers) and offer a Vampire Fang.	#
vc.codex.vampire.skills.2=Use the §4Blood Chalice§r to cast. §fSneak + use§r casts the selected skill instantly — great on mobile.	#
vc.codex.vampire.skills.title=Skills	#
vc.codex.vampire.sun.1=Under direct sunlight you burn. Young vampires suffer more; elders resist. A helmet, rain or a roof protects you.	#
vc.codex.vampire.sun.2=Running water hurts you unless you have §fWaterproof Skin§r. Sleep in a §fcoffin§r to skip the day.	#
vc.codex.vampire.sun.title=Sun and water	#
vc.codex.version=§8Version %s	#
vc.codex.werewolf.become.1=Use a §fWerewolf Fang§r (dropped by werewolves). The change takes 5 minutes — milk cancels it.	#
vc.codex.werewolf.become.2=As a werewolf you still need food, and the beast form makes you hungrier.	#
vc.codex.werewolf.become.title=Becoming a werewolf	#
vc.codex.werewolf.form.1=At dusk you transform. Use §fTransformation§r on the Moon Totem to toggle. Under a §ffull moon§r the beast can't be held back.	#
vc.codex.werewolf.form.2=In beast form you're fast, jump high, hit hard and see in the dark. At dawn you return to human.	#
vc.codex.werewolf.form.title=The beast form	#
vc.codex.werewolf.intro=§7Humans cursed by the moon.	#
vc.codex.werewolf.level.1=Earn experience by hunting — much more in beast form. Supernatural creatures are worth more.	#
vc.codex.werewolf.level.2=From level 3 you are faster at night even in human form.	#
vc.codex.werewolf.level.title=Levels	#
vc.codex.werewolf.skills.1=Fill the §4Blood Altar§r and offer a Werewolf Fang to awaken powers like Howl, Lunge and Brutal Blow.	#
vc.codex.werewolf.skills.2=§fSneak + use§r the Moon Totem to cast the selected skill without the menu.	#
vc.codex.werewolf.skills.title=Skills	#
vc.codex.werewolf.tiers.1=Your beast has 3 forms (I, II, III), unlocked at levels 1, 4 and 8. Each form changes your look and power.	#
vc.codex.werewolf.tiers.2=Defeating stronger werewolves may awaken the next form early.	#
vc.codex.werewolf.tiers.title=Beast evolution	#
vc.codex.world.bloodmoon.1=Some full moons become §4Blood Moons§r: the sky turns red, monsters get stronger and vampires ambush humans.	#
vc.codex.world.bloodmoon.2=Vampires and werewolves become much stronger during the event.	#
vc.codex.world.bloodmoon.title=Blood Moon	#
vc.codex.world.commands.1=/function sunrise/transvp, /translb, /transhunter — transform. /function sunrise/removevp — cure. /function sunrise/bloodmoon — Blood Moon.	#
vc.codex.world.commands.2=Advanced: /scriptevent vc:level 10, vc:blood 20, vc:skills all, vc:infect vampire. Give the §fvc_admin§r tag to access Administration.	#
vc.codex.world.commands.title=Commands	#
vc.codex.world.drops.1=Human hearts: hunters, pillagers and evokers; villagers only drop them when killed by vampires or werewolves. Fangs and blood come from vampires; livers and fangs from werewolves.	#
vc.codex.world.drops.2=Looting increases rare drops. The Blood Altar can also be found in crypts, towers and lunar circles, or dropped by Vampire Witches and Alpha Werewolves.	#
vc.codex.world.drops.title=Drops and relics	#
vc.codex.world.explore.1=Far from spawn (over 220 blocks) the world reacts: §6wolf packs§r and §4vampire nests§r at night, §ehunter patrols§r by day, §5witch covens§r and §fforgotten graves§r with chests.	#
vc.codex.world.explore.2=Look for underground §fVampire Crypts§r (with a Blood Altar and a vampire spawner), §fLunar Circles§r in taigas, towers, graveyards and hunter camps.	#
vc.codex.world.explore.title=Exploration	#
vc.codex.world.intro=§7Events, places and creatures.	#
vc.codex.world.mobs.1=Vampires burn in the sun and, when wounded, turn into bats to escape. Werewolves hunt at night and vanish at dawn.	#
vc.codex.world.mobs.2=There are also §fVampire Chickens§r and §fShadow Bats§r at night. Every add-on creature appears equally often. Undead ignore vampires and werewolves; iron golems attack them.	#
vc.codex.world.mobs.title=Creatures	#
vc.codex.world.structures.1=Look for §fvampire towers§r in dark forests, §fhunter camps§r (home of the §eHunter Master§r), §fhunter houses§r and §fgraveyards§r.	#
vc.codex.world.structures.2=Sunstone ore appears between layers 0 and 96; Moonstone deep in the deepslate. Every structure holds chests with relics.	#
vc.codex.world.structures.title=Structures	#
